# Per-experiment tooling-PATH env — TEMPLATE (tracked). Copy to `experiment.env` (gitignored) and fill
# in the real machine paths. This file holds ONLY machine-specific tooling PATHS that are shared by ALL
# arms of the experiment (a constant input, not per-arm assistance): the mlc model-ladder checkout and
# the external model/HW repos the oracle needs. NO per-arm content, NO answers, NO target logic — those
# stay in the target contract / capsule corpus / bundle manifests.
#
# The harness auto-sources `targets/<target>/experiment.env` into the environment before a run
# (merlin/experiments/capsule_bench/harness/_common.py); the process environment always WINS, so an
# exported var is never overridden. KEY=VALUE lines, `#` comments.
#
# Why this exists: `MERLIN_MLC_DIR` being absent is exactly what made the external-backend arc oracle
# read as unavailable (a gradeable run then scores 0/N with no actionable feedback). Setting it here — in
# ONE place shared by every arm — is the fix, and keeps machine paths out of tracked code.

# The mlc model-ladder checkout (arc models + CIRCT facts). Resolved by merlin.targetgen.rtl.mlc_bridge.
# Derivation hint: the sibling mvp-lhwir/modeling checkout that carries runs/circt-arc/<target>/.
MERLIN_MLC_DIR=/path/to/mvp-lhwir/modeling

# The model project whose venv lays out fp8/bf16 operands + owns the independent golden (runner.model_ext
# in the contract resolves MERLIN_EXT_<MODEL_EXT>). Derivation hint: the npu-model package inside atlas-npu.
MERLIN_EXT_NPU_MODEL=/path/to/mvp-lhwir/modeling/third_party/atlas-npu/npu-model

# The atlas-npu HW/generator repo (ISA definition + example kernels), via setup_atlas.py.
MERLIN_EXT_ATLAS_NPU=/path/to/mvp-lhwir/modeling/third_party/atlas-npu

# The chipyard checkout that elaborates the atlas SoC (cycle-accurate cross-check when wired).
MERLIN_EXT_CHIPYARD_ATLAS=/path/to/chipyard-atlas
